{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-342492",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14229051/assets/66b91f732d36469ded18df5404b3f12dddad7474168efd47ddf038835b67b831.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(-2x+1)=-2(-3)+1=7\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}({x}^{2}+1)=(3)^{2}+1=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14229051/assets/888053858d845bd47a56b953a5eb9a6f7f6b4ddffc0ecc70fa280e1a7d543f24.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-342492\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Let's examine the given statements in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Statement I is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"206\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"border: solid 1pt gainsboro;\"><mjx-mpadded><mjx-block style=\"width: 2.581em; margin: 0.4em 0px; position: relative;\"><mjx-rbox style=\"left: 0.4em; top: 0px; max-width: 2.581em;\"><mjx-mtext class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c74\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c72\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c75\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c65\"></mjx-c></mjx-mtext></mjx-rbox></mjx-block></mjx-mpadded></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle style=\"border: solid 1pt gainsboro\"><mpadded height=\"+4pt\" depth=\"+4pt\" lspace=\"4pt\" width=\"+8pt\"><mtext>true</mtext></mpadded></mstyle><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> The function <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"207\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is continuous on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax Ctxt